---
description: Types live in src/types (declarations only); Zod schemas live under features/*/validator only
alwaysApply: true
---

# Types vs validators

- **`src/types/*.ts`** — **TypeScript declarations only** (`type`, `interface`). No Zod, no runtime schemas. Examples: `@/types/loans`, `@/types/auth`, `@/types/global`.
- **`src/features/<name>/validator/`** — **Zod schemas** for that domain. Schemas import `type` shapes from `@/types/...`. Shared primitives for a domain (e.g. `nonEmptyStringSchema` under auth) stay in that feature’s `validator/` folder — do not use `src/lib/validation`.

## Imports

- Domain types: `import type { Loan } from "@/types/loans"`.
- Domain validation: `import { loanSchema } from "@/features/loans/validator/loan"`.

Do not add `validator/` under `src/types/` or validation modules under `src/lib/`.
